-- title:
--   The two-copy correlation is a product of conditional projections
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ne0$, let $\nu:\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z\to\mathbb R$, and let $H_0,H_1$ be two weighted simplex systems on $n+1$ copies of that group. Their two-copy centered correlation at a face $j$ is the normalized mean of the AP centered core at $j$ times the product of their projected weights at $j$.
